<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sue Harukata</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1521–1555</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Sue Takafusa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sue Harukata was a senior retainer of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ouchi-clan">Ōuchi clan</a> of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> who rebelled against his lord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ouchi-yoshitaka">Ōuchi Yoshitaka</a> in 1551, forcing him to suicide and installing a puppet. In 1555 Mōri Motonari defeated him at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-miyajima">Battle of Miyajima</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/itsukushima">Itsukushima</a>), where he killed himself, opening the way for Mōri control of the Ōuchi lands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sue-harukata.jpg" alt="Sue Harukata" width="320" height="328" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 緑亭川柳輯・前北斎卍老人 他 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sue_Harukata_by_Zoku_Eiyu_Hyakunin_Isshu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
